source/reference_guide/report.rst:79: (localised) ["localized", "localism"] : the number of cells the residual is effectively spread over. Equal to the cell count when every cell contributes equally, and to 1 when a single cell carries everything. A small value against a large mesh means a localised stall, not a stalled field.
